	(text "The RP2350 microcontrollers that are used are 5V tolerant, but only while it is powered.\nRegulator U1002 ensures that if the +3V3 rail loses power before the +5V rail, the +3V3\nrail is powered through the +5V rail until the +5V rail drops out, ensuring that the\nmicrocontrollers will at most be 0.5V below the +5V rail."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
